      "general": {
        "abstract": "Small agricultural catchment (91 ha) in a vineyard Mediterranean environment with 20 years of data: impact of global change (climate and anthropogenic activities as agricultural practices) on water and erosion balance, fluxes and quality. \r\nSoils: calcisoils and cambisoils. Bedrock: Marine and coastal miocene deposits. \r\nContinuous automatic measurements at nested scales from plot to catchment outlet (surface runoff, shallow groundwaters, surface-atmosphere fluxes) and continuous monitoring of anthropogenic activities   . \r\nMore information available on http://www.obs-omere.org.\r\nRoujan experimental catchment belongs to the French SOERE-RBV Network. ",
